# Allowlist: Vercel deploys ONLY the files listed below; everything else in
# the repo root is ignored.
#
# Previously this was a blocklist, and anything not named here was served
# publicly on the production domain — including CLAUDE.md (internal notes
# with client PII and infrastructure details), permissions-rls.sql,
# supabase/migrations/*, and _archive/* (whose blocklist entries didn't
# even match the real filenames). A new file added to the repo should be
# private by default, not public by default.
#
# Adding a page or script the site actually loads? Add it here too, or it
# will 404 in production.
#
# Note on the Railway backend files (package.json, server.js, etc.): they
# must stay excluded — package.json's "express" dependency and "start"
# script make Vercel auto-detect the repo as an Express app and deploy
# server.js instead of the static HTML. The allowlist excludes them
# implicitly.

/*

# Pages (reset-password and accept-invite are reached from email links)
!/index.html
!/login.html
!/signup.html
!/reset-password.html
!/accept-invite.html
!/admin-portal.html
!/client-portal.html

# Scripts
!/supabase.js
!/i18n.js
!/admin-portal-data.js
!/client-portal-data.js

# Static assets
!/assets

# Vercel config (security headers + CSP) — read by Vercel, not served
!/vercel.json
